oolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback worked and checkout-api is healthy on v2.3.0 (error rate 0.002). The incident call returned a 502 with a truncated body, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01P8q1rrW8XpmrXYgRe2nV1t", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is the failing release, so I didn't use v2.2.9. Because v2.3.0 has previously been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Incident:** SEV2 incident **INC-0001** is open for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, and the follow-ups. The first incident call returned a 502 with a truncated response, so I checked the incident list before doing anything else. It showed INC-0001 already created, so I didn't open a duplicate.\n\nv2.3.1 stays undeployed. Its staging build (v2.3.1-rc) is also marked unhealthy, so it needs investigation before any redeploy.", "type": "text"}]}]}